# Anything that mustn't end up inside the backend image.
#
# Why this exists: backend/Dockerfile does `COPY . /app` in both the `dev`
# and `runtime` stages. Without this list, the local working tree leaks into
# the image — including the `.env` you keep next to docker-compose for local
# development, Python venvs, test fixtures, and editor metadata. The image
# is pushed to a private ECR, but defence-in-depth: secrets do not belong in
# container layers, period (image layers are world-readable inside ECR, and
# anything that can `docker pull` extracts them).

# Local dev secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python build / cache artefacts (rebuilt fresh inside the image)
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Local storage / data dirs (Lightsail uses S3 in prod)
data
storage
*.sqlite
*.db

# Build / IDE / OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log

# Tests are needed for the `dev` stage but not for `runtime`. Listing them
# here would break the dev image; keep them in. The `pytest_cache` line above
# strips only the cache directory, not the tests themselves.
